sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To circumscribe about a given circle a triangle equiangular with a given triangle.
----
proof:

Let {ABC} be the given circle, and {DEF} the given triangle.

It is required to circumscribe a triangle equiangular with the triangle {DEF} about the circle {ABC}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="360" height="290" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IV.3 diagram" src="propIV3.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // EF produced both ways, the centre K and a radius KB, the I.23 angle
    // copies at K, the three tangents, then the angle sums: the
    // quadrilateral AMBK for the angle at M, "similarly" BNCK for the angle
    // at N, and I.32 for the angle at L.
    //
    // Joyce's figure builds A and C from the triangle (`similar` points
    // A' and C', cut off on the radius), and M, N, L as the crossings of
    // the perpendiculars at A, B, C, so it follows the proof's order as it
    // stands. ABC is the circle's edge with no face; ABCdup, a faceless-edge
    // twin, carries the fill above LMN.
    //
    // Everything added leaves the resting figure as it was. EF (the side
    // the proof produces), KM (the diagonal that divides AMBK into two
    // triangles) and the quadrilaterals AMBK and BNCK are transparent
    // highlight targets. FH, KB, KA, KC, LM, MN and NL are solid black
    // lines over Joyce's HF, BK, AK, CK and the sides of LMN, hidden at rest
    // (initiallyHidden) and used by the slides instead: they run in the
    // direction the construction draws them — F out to H, K out to the
    // circumference — and give the three tangents strokes of their own
    // before LMN's face lands on the closing slides.
    //
    // Angle markers: equal angles share a colour — DEG and AKB blue, DFH
    // and BKC green, DEF and AMB purple, DFE and LNB orange, EDF and MLN
    // teal. The right angles at A, B, C (III.18) are red squares. Markers
    // at a shared vertex here lie side by side (E, F, K, B), not nested, so
    // they are pinned to opt out of same-vertex ring stepping.
    var GIVEN = ["ABC","ABCdup","DEF","D","E","F"];
    var PROD  = GIVEN.concat(["EF","EG","FH","G","H"]);
    var CEN   = PROD.concat(["K"]);
    var RAD   = CEN.concat(["KB","B"]);
    var ANG1  = RAD.concat(["angDEG","KA","A","angAKB"]);
    var ANG2  = ANG1.concat(["angDFH","KC","C","angBKC"]);
    var TAN   = ANG2.concat(["LM","MN","NL","L","M","N"]);
    var RIGHT = TAN.concat(["rtKAM","rtKBM","rtKBN","rtKCN"]);
    var QUAD  = RIGHT.concat(["AMBK"]);
    var SPLIT = QUAD.concat(["KM"]);
    // KM was transitory: dropped once the two triangles have been named.
    var SUM   = QUAD.concat(["angM"]);
    var DEFS  = SUM.concat(["angE"]);
    var SIM   = DEFS.concat(["BNCK","angN","angF"]);
    var REM   = SIM.concat(["angL","angD"]);
    var DONE  = REM.concat(["LMN"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IV.3",
        elements: [
            "B;point;free;160,120",
            "K;point;free;120,150",
            "BK;line;connect;B,K",
            "ABC;circle;radius;K,B;0;0;black;0",
            "D;point;free;320,55",
            "E;point;free;230,150",
            "F;point;free;220,55",
            "DEF;polygon;triangle;D,E,F;0;0;black;random",
            "H;point;lineSlider;E,F,220,30",
            "G;point;lineSlider;E,F,260,220",
            "HF;line;connect;H,F",
            "EG;line;connect;E,G",
            "A';point;similar;B,K,G,E,D;0;0",
            "A;point;cutoff;K,A',K,B",
            "AK;line;connect;A,K",
            "C';point;similar;B,K,H,F,D;0;0",
            "C;point;cutoff;K,C',K,B",
            "CK;line;connect;C,K",
            "Atan;line;perpendicular;A,K;0;0;0",
            "Btan;line;perpendicular;B,K;0;0;0",
            "Ctan;line;perpendicular;C,K;0;0;0",
            "M;point;intersection;Atan,Btan",
            "N;point;intersection;Btan,Ctan",
            "L;point;intersection;Ctan,Atan",
            "LMN;polygon;triangle;L,M,N;0;0;black;random",
            "ABCdup;circle;radius;K,B;0;0;0;random",
            // The side the proof produces.
            "EF;line;connect;E,F;0;0;0",
            // Slide twins of HF, BK, AK, CK and the sides of LMN, hidden at
            // rest (see above).
            "FH;line;connect;F,H",
            "KB;line;connect;K,B",
            "KA;line;connect;K,A",
            "KC;line;connect;K,C",
            "LM;line;connect;L,M",
            "MN;line;connect;M,N",
            "NL;line;connect;N,L",
            // The quadrilaterals and the diagonal of AMBK. Explicit ;0 faces.
            "KM;line;connect;K,M;0;0;0",
            "AMBK;polygon;quadrilateral;A,M,B,K;0;0;0;0",
            "BNCK;polygon;quadrilateral;B,N,C,K;0;0;0;0",
            "angDEG;sector;angleMarker;E,D,G,22;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angE;sector;angleMarker;E,D,F,22;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angDFH;sector;angleMarker;F,D,H,22;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angF;sector;angleMarker;F,D,E,22;0;0;c06a1b;f3c590",
            "angD;sector;angleMarker;D,E,F;0;0;2a8a8a;9fdcdc",
            "angAKB;sector;angleMarker;K,A,B,22;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angBKC;sector;angleMarker;K,B,C,22;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angM;sector;angleMarker;M,A,B;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angN;sector;angleMarker;N,C,B;0;0;c06a1b;f3c590",
            "angL;sector;angleMarker;L,M,N;0;0;2a8a8a;9fdcdc",
            "rtKAM;sector;angleMarkerRight;A,K,M,16;0;0;red;red",
            "rtKBM;sector;angleMarkerRight;B,K,M,16;0;0;red;red",
            "rtKBN;sector;angleMarkerRight;B,K,N,16;0;0;red;red",
            "rtKCN;sector;angleMarkerRight;C,K,N,16;0;0;red;red"
        ],
        // Draggables (checked against the bundle): B, K, D, E, F free; G, H
        // lineSliders on EF. D, E, F are the given triangle and stand from
        // slide 1. G and H arrive when EF is produced, K when the centre is
        // taken, B with the radius drawn "at random", so those four are
        // deferred and follow `visible`. A, C (cutoff) and L, M, N
        // (intersection) are derived and listed per slide. The resting
        // figure is unaffected.
        deferDraggables: ["G","H","K","B"],
        initiallyHidden: ["FH","KB","KA","KC","LM","MN","NL"],
        // The triangle owns DEF; the angle DEF takes {DEF|angE}.
        aliases: { "FE": "EF", "GE": "EG", "HF": "FH",
                   "BK": "KB", "AK": "KA", "CK": "KC",
                   "LAM": "LM", "ML": "LM", "MBN": "MN", "NM": "MN",
                   "NCL": "NL", "LN": "NL", "MK": "KM",
                   "BKA": "angAKB", "AKB": "angAKB",
                   "BKC": "angBKC", "CKB": "angBKC",
                   "DEG": "angDEG", "GED": "angDEG",
                   "DFH": "angDFH", "HFD": "angDFH",
                   "DFE": "angF", "EFD": "angF",
                   "EDF": "angD", "FDE": "angD",
                   "AMB": "angM", "BMA": "angM",
                   "LNB": "angN", "BNL": "angN",
                   "MLN": "angL", "NLM": "angL",
                   "KAM": "rtKAM", "MAK": "rtKAM",
                   "KBM": "rtKBM", "MBK": "rtKBM" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To circumscribe about a given circle a triangle equiangular with a given triangle.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABC","DEF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "IV.3" }] },
            { text: "Let {ABC} be the given circle, and {DEF} the given triangle.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["ABC","DEF"] },
            { text: "It is required to circumscribe a triangle equiangular with the triangle {DEF} about the circle {ABC}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["DEF","ABC"] },
            { text: "Produce {EF} in both directions to the points {G} and {H}.",
              visible: PROD,
              highlighted: ["EF","G","H"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "EG", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "G",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "FH", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "H",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.2" }] },
            { text: "Take the center {K} of the circle {ABC},",
              visible: CEN,
              highlighted: ["K"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "K", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "III.1" }] },
            { text: "and draw a radius {KB} at random.",
              visible: RAD,
              highlighted: ["KB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "KB", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "B",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "On the straight line {KB} and at the point {K} on it, construct the angle {BKA} equal to the angle {DEG},",
              visible: ANG1,
              highlighted: ["KB","K"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angDEG", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "KA",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "A",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "angAKB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle BKA = angle DEG", ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "and the angle {BKC} equal to the angle {DFH}.",
              visible: ANG2,
              highlighted: ["KB","K"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angDFH", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "KC",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "C",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "angBKC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle BKC = angle DFH", ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "Through the points {A}, {B}, and {C} draw {LAM}, {MBN}, and {NCL} touching the circle {ABC}.",
              visible: TAN,
              highlighted: ["A","B","C"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "LM", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "MN", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "NL", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "at right angles to the radii at A, B, C", ref: "III.16,Cor" }] },
            { text: "Now, since {LM}, {MN}, and {NL} touch the circle {ABC} at the points {A}, {B}, and {C},",
              visible: TAN,
              highlighted: ["LM","MN","NL","A","B","C"] },
            { text: "and {KA}, {KB}, and {KC} have been joined from the center {K} to the points {A}, {B}, and {C},",
              visible: TAN,
              highlighted: ["KA","KB","KC","K"] },
            { text: "therefore the angles at the points {A}, {B}, and {C} are right.",
              visible: RIGHT,
              highlighted: ["rtKAM","rtKBM","rtKBN","rtKCN"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "rtKAM", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtKBM", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtKBN", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtKCN", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "a radius to the point of contact is perpendicular to the tangent", ref: "III.18" }] },
            { text: "And, since the four angles of the quadrilateral {AMBK} equal four right angles,",
              visible: QUAD,
              highlighted: ["AMBK"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "AMBK", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] } },
            { text: "inasmuch as {AMBK} is in fact divisible into two triangles,",
              visible: SPLIT,
              highlighted: ["AMBK","KM"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "KM", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "the angles of each triangle equal two right angles", ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "and the angles {KAM} and {KBM} are right,",
              visible: QUAD,
              highlighted: ["rtKAM","rtKBM"] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the remaining angles {AKB} and {AMB} equals two right angles.",
              visible: SUM,
              highlighted: ["angAKB","angM"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angM", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "take away the right angles at A and B", ref: "C.N.3" }] },
            { text: "But the sum of the angles {DEG} and {DEF|angE} also equals two right angles,",
              visible: DEFS,
              highlighted: ["angDEG","angE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angles DEG and DEF on the straight line GF", ref: "I.13" }] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the angles {AKB} and {AMB} equals the sum of the angles {DEG} and {DEF|angE},",
              visible: DEFS,
              highlighted: ["angAKB","angM","angDEG","angE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "each sum equals two right angles", ref: "C.N.1" }] },
            { text: "of which the angle {AKB} equals the angle {DEG},",
              visible: DEFS,
              highlighted: ["angAKB","angDEG"] },
            { text: "therefore the remaining angle {AMB} equals the remaining angle {DEF|angE}.",
              visible: DEFS,
              highlighted: ["angM","angE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "take away the equal angles AKB and DEG", ref: "C.N.3" }] },
            { text: "Similarly it can be proved that the angle {LNB} also equals the angle {DFE},",
              visible: SIM,
              highlighted: ["BNCK","angN","angF"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angN", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the remaining angle {MLN} equals the angle {EDF}.",
              visible: REM,
              highlighted: ["angL","angD"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angL", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "the three angles of a triangle equal two right angles", ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the triangle {LMN} is equiangular with the triangle {DEF},",
              visible: DONE,
              highlighted: ["angL","angM","angN","angD","angE","angF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "LMN", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and it has been circumscribed about the circle {ABC}.",
              visible: DONE,
              highlighted: ["LM","MN","NL","ABC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "each side of LMN touches the circle", ref: "IV.Def.4" }] },
            { text: "Therefore a triangle equiangular with the given triangle has been circumscribed about a given circle.",
              visible: DONE,
              highlighted: ["angL","angM","angN","angD","angE","angF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.F." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "IV.3") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1":   "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.Post.2":   "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post2/",
        "C.N.1":      "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn1/",
        "C.N.3":      "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn3/",
        "I.13":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI13/",
        "I.23":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI23/",
        "I.32":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI32/",
        "III.1":      "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII1/",
        "III.16,Cor": "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII16/#cor",
        "III.18":     "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII18/",
        "IV.Def.4":   "/elements/books/bookIV/definitions/defIV4/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

<div class="just"><a href="/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII1/">III.1</a><br><a href="/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI23/">I.23</a><br><a href="/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII16/#cor">III.16,Cor</a></div>

Produce {EF} in both directions to the points {G} and {H}. Take the center {K} of the circle {ABC}, and draw a radius {KB} at random. On the straight line {KB} and at the point {K} on it, construct the angle {BKA} equal to the angle {DEG}, and the angle {BKC} equal to the angle {DFH}. Through the points {A}, {B}, and {C} draw {LAM}, {MBN}, and {NCL} touching the circle {ABC}.

Now, since {LM}, {MN}, and {NL} touch the circle {ABC} at the points {A}, {B}, and {C}, and {KA}, {KB}, and {KC} have been joined from the center {K} to the points {A}, {B}, and {C}, therefore the angles at the points {A}, {B}, and {C} are right. [!just III.18]

And, since the four angles of the quadrilateral {AMBK} equal four right angles, inasmuch as {AMBK} is in fact divisible into two triangles, and the angles {KAM} and {KBM} are right, therefore the sum of the remaining angles {AKB} and {AMB} equals two right angles.

But the sum of the angles {DEG} and {DEF|angE} also equals two right angles, therefore the sum of the angles {AKB} and {AMB} equals the sum of the angles {DEG} and {DEF|angE}, of which the angle {AKB} equals the angle {DEG}, therefore the remaining angle {AMB} equals the remaining angle {DEF|angE}. [!just I.13]

Similarly it can be proved that the angle {LNB} also equals the angle {DFE}, therefore the remaining angle {MLN} equals the angle {EDF}. [!just I.32]

Therefore the triangle {LMN} is equiangular with the triangle {DEF}, and it has been circumscribed about the circle {ABC}. [!just IV.Def.4]

Therefore a triangle equiangular with the given triangle has been circumscribed about a given circle.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
----
guide: This proposition is not used elsewhere in the *Elements,* but is included as a mate to the previous proposition in which a triangle is inscribed inside rather than circumscribed outside a given circle.
